hi Richard,
With respect to your first question, "occasion" refers to a
survey-specific covariate (hence it falls into the obsCov or
observation-level bracket).  Since sites are assumed to be closed to
changes in occupancy within years, these obsCovs can only influence
detection.  You tried to model site extinction as a function of
occasion, but unmarked wouldn't let you because sites cannot go
extinct within a year.  The model fm <- colext(~1, ~1, ~1, ~occasion,
umf) will run.

Hope this helps,
Brittany
