Richard,

Thanks for the reply and suggestions, I was worried I was way off base.
 Providing the starting values you suggested resulted in abundance and
detection probability estimates that seam reasonable.  I have a few
sites that are close where I have conducted a multi-pass depletion
survey of smallmouth bass the past 2 years.  Using the Bayesian
probability model for closed populations under unequal catchability
described by Mantyniemi et al. (2005) I get first pass detection
probabilities between 0.20 and 0.40 compared to 0.27 with the limited
sites above.  The depletion sites are only 200m long but if I expand
their estimates to 1000m (the distance for the sites above) I get 417 fish/km which is very close to the 351 fish/km estimated for the same year above.

Thanks for the help,
Jason

